286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 684 0 R
/ActualText (The Render Props pattern in React allows components to share reusable logic. It involves passing a function \(known as a "render prop"\) to a component, which uses it to determine what to render.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 685 0 R
/ActualText (This pattern provides a more flexible way to share logic between components without relying on Higher-Order Components \(HOCs\) or tightly coupling functionality to specific components.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 686 0 R
/ActualText (How Does Render Props Work?)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 687 0 R
/ActualText (A render prop is essentially a function prop that a component uses to know what content or JSX to display. This function gives control to the consuming component over how the data or state inside the component is rendered.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
